        "answer": {
          "short": "a: Lower quartile position $25.5$; median position $50.5$; upper quartile position $75.5$.",
          "worked": "For 100 ordered values, the lower half occupies positions 1–50 and the upper half positions 51–100.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Lower quartile position}&=\\frac{25+26}{2}\\\\\\text{Lower quartile position}&=25.5\\\\\\text{Median position}&=\\frac{50+51}{2}\\\\\\text{Median position}&=50.5\\\\\\text{Upper quartile position}&=\\frac{75+76}{2}\\\\\\text{Upper quartile position}&=75.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "b: Lower quartile position $25.5$; median position $51$; upper quartile position $76.5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median position}&=\\frac{101+1}{2}\\\\\\text{Median position}&=51\\end{align*}$$\nOmit position 51 when dividing the ordered data into halves. The lower half occupies positions 1–50 and the upper half positions 52–101.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Lower quartile position}&=\\frac{25+26}{2}\\\\\\text{Lower quartile position}&=25.5\\\\\\text{Upper quartile position}&=\\frac{76+77}{2}\\\\\\text{Upper quartile position}&=76.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
    ]
